WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:10.120
23. The Ancient Art of the Brush Throughout its long history, writing has been

2
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:15.820
a big deal in China. Since the earliest dynasties, the skills of reading and writing have been

3
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:22.640
highly respected. In fact, they form an important part of the Chinese art world. Calligraphy,

4
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.620
the art of writing with a brush, is almost as old as writing itself. And though this

5
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:33.580
art form dates back thousands of years, it is still extremely popular today.

6
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:38.900
How did writing become so important in Chinese culture? The answer most likely lies way back

7
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.700
in the Shang dynasty, about 1600 to 1046 B.C. That's when characters were first carved

8
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:51.060
in bronze and used in religious events. This practice conveyed a spiritual aspect which

9
00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:57.100
gave writing authority in the eyes of ordinary people. Calligraphy spread during the Han

10
00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:02.900
dynasty, when the necessary tools and materials became more widely available. First there

11
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:09.120
was the brush, made from bamboo and animal hair. Early ink, or lamp black, was made by

12
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.540
burning pine wood and mixing it with water. Early forms of paper were invented around

13
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:22.540
AD 105. Finally, there was inkstone, a smooth piece of stone used for mixing ink. Together,

14
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:28.020
these tools were known as the four treasures of study in ancient China. Calligraphy has

15
00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:33.020
been popular in China for thousands of years. Some say that it's an even higher art form

16
00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:38.420
than painting. Though foreigners may not always get it, there's something truly special about

17
00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:44.460
calligraphy. Every written character has a strict stroke order. When viewing the results,

18
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:50.580
you can trace the artist's process, reliving every stroke of his or her brush. This allows

19
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:56.100
for an intimate connection between artist and audience. Calligraphy is something that's best

20
00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:02.380
experienced by doing. Luckily, this ancient art is still widely practiced today. So,

21
00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:06.060
what are you waiting for? Get out there and find yourself a teacher.
